=head1 ServiceInstance

See also L<Twilio::InstanceResource>.

It has C<fetch>, C<update>, C<delete>, C<access_tokens>, C<approve_challenge>,
C<entities>, C<messaging_configurations>, C<new_challenge>, C<new_factors>,
C<new_verify_factors>, C<rate_limits>, C<verifications>, C<verification_checks>
and C<webhooks>, which work as they do on the context.

Its fields are:

=over

=item account_sid

The SID of the L<Account|https://www.twilio.com/docs/iam/api/account> that
created the Service resource.

=item code_length

The length of the verification code to generate.

=item custom_code_enabled

Whether to allow sending verifications with a custom code instead of a randomly
generated one.

=item date_created

The date and time in GMT when the resource was created specified in L<RFC
2822|https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc2822.txt> format. A L<Time::Piece> object in
UTC. See L<Twilio::Deserialize/date_time>.

=item date_updated

The date and time in GMT when the resource was last updated specified in L<RFC
2822|https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc2822.txt> format. A L<Time::Piece> object in
UTC. See L<Twilio::Deserialize/date_time>.

=item default_template_sid

No description in the specification.

=item do_not_share_warning_enabled

Whether to add a security warning at the end of an SMS verification body.
Disabled by default and applies only to SMS. Example SMS body: C<Your AppName
verification code is: 1234. Don’t share this code with anyone; our employees
will never ask for the code>

=item dtmf_input_required

Whether to ask the user to press a number before delivering the verify code in
a phone call.

=item friendly_name

The name that appears in the body of your verification messages. It can be up
to 30 characters long and can include letters, numbers, spaces, dashes,
underscores. Phone numbers, special characters or links are NOT allowed. It
cannot contain more than 4 (consecutive or non-consecutive) digits. B<This
value should not contain PII.>

=item links

The URLs of related resources.

=item lookup_enabled

Whether to perform a lookup with each verification started and return info
about the phone number.

=item passkeys

No description in the specification.

=item psd2_enabled

Whether to pass PSD2 transaction parameters when starting a verification.

=item push

Configurations for the Push factors (channel) created under this Service.

=item sid

The unique string that we created to identify the Service resource.

=item skip_sms_to_landlines

Whether to skip sending SMS verifications to landlines. Requires
C<lookup_enabled>.

=item totp

Configurations for the TOTP factors (channel) created under this Service.

=item tts_name

The name of an alternative text-to-speech service to use in phone calls.
Applies only to TTS languages.

=item url

The absolute URL of the resource.

=item verify_event_subscription_enabled

Whether to allow verifications from the service to reach the stream-events
sinks if configured

=item whatsapp

No description in the specification.

=back

